 "ios-actions|Toolbars": {
  "summary": "A Plenix toolbar on iOS is the system toolbar and navigation bar (.toolbar, UINavigationBar, UIToolbar), kept native in its glass background, standard corner radii, Back and Close buttons, overflow, scroll edge behavior and VoiceOver order. Plenix sets its content and type: a short title in DM Sans at the heading role (a large title at the title role on top-level views), borderless SF Symbols in the Plenix content color instead of the system tint, at most one primary action in the Plenix primary color at the trailing end, and no more than three groups. Apple’s default draws SF Pro titles and tinted items; Plenix keeps the bar and changes the type and the item colors.",
